आध्यत्मिक",
      "textEn": "378\nChetan--consciousness or logic; Hridayam--in the heart; Chaitya--the presiding deity of consciousness; Kshetra-j--knowing the field;\nPravisht--entered; Yada--when; Virat--the cosmic being; Tada--then; Ev--he; Purushah--the cosmic being; Salilat--from water;\nUdatiishta--arose \\.\n\nBut when the presiding deity of consciousness, the regulator of the inner self, entered the heart with logic,\nAt that very moment, the cosmic being rose up from the abode of the causal ocean. Just as a person who is asleep is awakened by the breath,\nSo are those who are born without effort. 79>. Meaning of the word\n\nYatha-- as; Prasuptam-- asleep; Purusham-- man; Prana-- life-air; Indriya-- organs of action and knowledge; Shat-- as many;\nManah-- mind; Dhihyah- intellect; Prabhavanti- are capable; Vina- without; Yena- by which; Na- not;\nUththapayitum- to lift up; Ojasah- with one's power.\n.\n\nWhen a man is asleep, all his physical possessions--such as vital energy,\nsense organs, motor organs, mind, and intellect--cannot inspire him. He can only be awakened\nwhen God helps him.\n\nMeaning: The explanation of Sankhya Darshan here has been elaborated from this perspective that\nthe cosmic form of the great man, that is, Shri Bhagavan, is the origin center of the various sense organs and their presiding deities.\nThe relationship between the great man and the sense organs, or the living beings, is so complex that merely by using the sense organs, their presiding deities cannot be awakened, even if they are mutually\nrelated. It is not possible to awaken a great man or connect God with worldly actions.\nOnly through devotion and detachment can one connect with the all-pervading God.\nIn that self-realization, with the mind engaged in yoga,\nWith devotion, detachment, and knowledge, contemplate the self. 72 Meaning of the word\n\nTam--On that; Asmin--In this; Pratyaksha--With the self; Paramatma--Supreme soul; Dhihya--With the mind; Yogapravrittaya--Engaged in devotion;\nBhaktya--Through devotion; Viraktya--With detachment; Gyanena--Through knowledge; Vivichya- While carefully considering;\nAtmani-In the body; Chintayet-One should contemplate; Chintayit-One should contemplate;Therefore, through dedication, detachment, and focused devotion, a person attains spirituality"
